"make check" runs the whole suite against a local server (run_tests.sh):
the server listens on the fixed endpoint 2001 for ncacn_ip_tcp and
ncadg_ip_udp, then perf_tcp.sh and perf_udp.sh run the client tests.
The tests that need the endpoint mapper are skipped unless rpcd is
running; the UDP broadcast test (3) only runs with PERF_BROADCAST=1.
PERF_SKIP lists more tests to skip, PERF_TIMEOUT limits each test
(default 120 seconds); see the comments in run_tests.sh and perf_tcp.sh.

